            <ArticleTitle>Kawasaki disease without fever.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>927-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/INF.0b013e3181a81cf0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Kawasaki disease (KD) characteristically presents with prolonged, remittent fever in addition to other clinical findings. We report the case of a 3-month-old boy who developed characteristic manifestations of KD and coronary aneurysms in the absence of fever. This case report underlines the difficulty to diagnose KD in young infants.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
